# Build context exclusions.
#
# Without this file the context was 236 MB and climbing - node_modules, the
# Python virtualenv, Next.js build output, the 50 MB training corpus and every
# Docker layer cache, all uploaded to the daemon on every single build.
#
# Two consequences, and the second is the serious one:
#
#   1. Every build wasted minutes transferring files the Dockerfile discards.
#   2. `.env.production` holds real secrets - database password, JWT signing
#      key, storage credentials - and was inside the context. Any `COPY . .`
#      would have baked them into an image layer, where they survive even if a
#      later layer deletes the file. Images get shared; that is how secrets
#      leak.
#
# Anything the build genuinely needs must NOT be listed here.

# ── Secrets. Never in an image. ──────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/

# ── Dependencies, rebuilt inside the image ───────────────────────────
node_modules
**/node_modules
.venv
**/.venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc

# ── Build output, regenerated inside the image ───────────────────────
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Tool caches ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.turbo
**/.turbo
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
.import_linter_cache
.git
.github
.husky
.vscode
.idea

# ── Data and artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The training corpus is ~50 MB and the model is rebuilt by apps/ml, not by a
# container. Backups and reports have no business in an image at all.
apps/ml/datasets
apps/ml/reports
apps/ml/models
backups/
coverage/
htmlcov/
.coverage
test-results/
playwright-report/
**/test-results
**/playwright-report

# ── Docs and local scripts ───────────────────────────────────────────
docs/
*.md
!apps/ml/README.md
*.pdf
*.bat
testing/
